</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="Pt0.A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.1 </span>Toy Experiments</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Model Architecture and Configuration</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the toy experiments, the flow model is parameterized by a 4-layer Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP).
At inference, both configurations utilize an Euler ODE solver with <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> integration steps.
Throughout the process, the noise scale parameter is fixed at <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for all timesteps <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Measurement of Ground Truth Discrepancy</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To measure the Ground Truth (GT) discrepancy shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F2.sf3" title="Figure 2(c) ‣ Figure 2 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Training-Free Refinement of Flow Matching with Divergence-based Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(c)</span></a>, we utilize the full training dataset. By drawing a sufficiently large number of target data points (<math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=100,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=100,000</annotation></semantics></math>), we construct an empirical target distribution. Relying on the standard flow matching formulation, we can empirically define the exact optimal marginal velocity field, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, under the assumption that this empirical distribution represents the true target.
Consequently, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is analytically formulated as the conditional expectation marginalized over the <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> empirical target samples:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(x_{t}):=\frac{\sum_{k=1}^{N}p_{t}(x_{t}|x_{1}^{(k)})v_{t}(x_{t}\mid x_{1}^{(k)})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}p_{t}(x_{t}|x_{1}^{(j)})},\quad v_{t}(x_{t}\mid x_{1}^{(k)})=\frac{x_{1}^{(k)}-x_{t}}{1-t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(x_{t}):=\frac{\sum_{k=1}^{N}p_{t}(x_{t}|x_{1}^{(k)})v_{t}(x_{t}\mid x_{1}^{(k)})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}p_{t}(x_{t}|x_{1}^{(j)})},\quad v_{t}(x_{t}\mid x_{1}^{(k)})=\frac{x_{1}^{(k)}-x_{t}}{1-t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample from the empirical target distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.2 </span>Main Experiments</h3>

<figure id="Pt0.A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Pt0.A3.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A3.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Throughput across different configurations.<span id="Pt0.A3.T4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Values indicate the wall-clock generation time, measured in seconds per batch (sec./batch).</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="Pt0.A3.T4.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="Pt0.A3.T4.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
